  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760218,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1943: The Battle of Midway (NES) - Synopsis\n\nRelive the thrilling aerial combat of World War II in *1943: The Battle of Midway* for the Nintendo Entertainment System! This classic scrolling shooter, originally an arcade hit, puts you in the cockpit of a P-38 Lightning fighter plane, tasked with battling the Imperial Japanese Navy across 16 intense stages.  Inspired by the pivotal Battle of Midway, the game follows a nameless U.S. Navy ace on a mission of revenge, ultimately aiming to destroy the mighty battleship Yamato.\n\nExperience fast-paced, vertically scrolling gameplay reminiscent of its predecessor, *1942*. Utilize button 1 to fire your standard machine gun and button 2 for special lightning attacks or a signature loop maneuver. Collect power-ups to cycle through a variety of devastating weapons, including shotguns, auto-cannons, and powerful lasers.  A unique fuel meter system adds a layer of strategy, and a 2-player mode allows for cooperative action.  Due to sensitivities surrounding the original arcade version's portrayal of the conflict, the NES release features fictionalized names for warships and battlefields, softening the historical context."
    },
